Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||12-07-2000||09:58 AM||||If you clicked here, you either said, "Huh?" or are a true Baseball fan!<P>My kids just got a package from another family we've known for a few years. Inside, for my daughter was a small lamb stuffed animal, which, of course, I couldn't resist giving to my wife, and chanting "Mary has a little lamb...." Also inside was a baseball for my boy. It was inscribed (OK, written on...), "To Patrick, Best Wishes to a Great Fan (signed) Rico Petrocelli"<P>My friend is a Youth Pastor at a church where Rico is one of the Men's Group leaders. For those of you who are still saying, "Huh?" Rico played for the Impossible Dream team (The 1967 Red Sox; as a rookie, if I remember correctly), at least through the 1975 World Series (Possibly some of the best baseball ever played), when I started getting interested in Baseball. He was a shortstop who didn't whine when he got moved to third base, who played hard and always gave his all, even though he was overshadowed in popular opinion by veterans like Carl Yastremski and Luis Tiant, and up and coming rookies like Jim Rice (Another fave of mine. I wear #14) and Fred Lynn. He's also on the local AM Sports station, and always a gentleman, the way all sports players should be.<P>To my friends, Scott and Meme, I say thanks, and Wow! To Rico, though you probably won't be reading this on a Fiero message board, I was too young to remember a lot of the specifics, but you will always stand out in my mind as being the standard by which I measure the whining millionaires.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||frontal lobe||12-07-2000||12:17 PM||||I'm 44 y.o. and so when I was growing up I watched him play.  He was a good to at times all-star player back then.  I don't watch baseball much anymore because the players are SO overpaid, have such bad attitudes, and don't hustle (generalization, there are some exceptions) that I'm not really a fan anymore.<P>I'm glad to hear he is a nice person.||||reg||1
